  "notes": "plod: The salt tortoise: twice the height of an elephant (a shell 7.4 m long and 4.8 m high), its high domed shell bleached grey-white, plated with scutes whose growth rings show, the rim worn and nicked, and crusted with salt on the back and low down where it lies in the brine. A heavy wrinkled head on a thick neck, pillar legs with big scales on the front. A few of them cross the Mirror, very slowly, from the brine to the islands and back, and take no notice of anyone. When you come close it draws head, legs and tail in under the rim. Nobody knows how old they are.",
